/* 段落记忆 · 词层 3 · 子块 a：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(3,{"sub":"a","par":{"consume":{"tw":[["consumption",4],["drink",3],["exhaust",0],["spend",2],["waste",0],["destroy",2],["abstain",1]],"en":"The factory promised to consume less water. A study showed that its consumption was three times that of the whole town. Old machines would drink power all night and exhaust hot air into the street. Managers had to spend a large part of the budget on new pipes that waste no heat and destroy less material. One worker said the real problem was speed, not water. For a month the staff tried to abstain from overtime, and the numbers fell by half. A second study later found the saving was real.","zh":"这家厂承诺减少用水。一份研究显示，它的耗水量是整个镇子的三倍。旧机器整夜耗电，还把热风吹到街上。管理层只好拿出一大笔预算换新管道——不浪费热量，也少毁坏材料。有位工人说，真正的问题在速度，不在水。全体员工试着一个月不加班，数字就降了一半。后来的第二份研究证明，省下来的是真的。"},"compensate":{"tw":[["cover",3],["pay",2],["give",3],["recover",6],["settle",2],["recoup",3],["carry",3],["suffer",6],["right",0]],"en":"After the storm, the small shop had to compensate every family whose roof was damaged. The owner would cover the cost of glass and tiles out of his own pocket. He had to pay for two weeks of work and give tools to three helpers. Nobody in the village could recover the lost harvest, but the insurance company promised to settle the claims within a month. The owner hoped to recoup part of his money from the bank. He said he would rather carry the debt himself than let a neighbour suffer. That, he said, is the right way to do business.","zh":"暴风过后，那家小店得赔偿每一户屋顶受损的人家。老板自掏腰包买玻璃和瓦。他付了两周的工钱，还给三个帮手发了工具。村里谁也没法把损失的收成找回来，但保险公司答应一个月内把理赔结清。老板希望从银行那边收回一部分钱。他说，与其让邻居受苦，不如自己背着这笔债。他说，做生意就该这样才对。"},"component":{"tw":[["element",0],["member",3],["factor",0],["core",6],["ingredient",0],["compose",4],["dynamic",6],["basis",3]],"en":"Every part of a good machine has a job. One component may be cheap and another may cost as much as the whole frame, but each one is an element of the same design. A missing member of the team is often the real reason a project fails; the human factor matters more than the metal. The basis of the plan is that nothing should be hidden. The core idea of the new pump is simple: fewer parts and a better fit, and its main ingredient is a single ring that moves with the water. The engineers compose the list of parts on one page and test each small dynamic piece before it leaves the factory.","zh":"一台好机器上的每个零件都有它的用处。有的部件很便宜，有的贵得能顶整个机架，但每一个都是同一套设计里的组成部分。团队里少一个人，往往才是项目失败真正的原因——人的因素比金属更重要。方案的根本前提是：什么都不要藏着。新水泵的核心想法很简单：零件更少、配合更好，而它最主要的成分是一个随水移动的圆环。工程师把零件清单记在一页纸上，让每个小的运动件在出厂前都过一遍测试。"},"angle":{"tw":[["angler",4],["fish",2],["lead",3],["space",2],["velocity",6],["angular",4],["weight",0],["list",3],["travel",2],["curve",6],["lean",0]],"en":"At dawn the angler stood in the cold river and studied the angle of his line. He knew that the weight of a big fish would bend the rod into a deep curve. A strong pull could make the small boat list to one side, so he kept his feet wide and his body lean. Each cast would lead the hook into a quiet space near the reeds, where the water had almost no velocity. The line would travel slowly downstream, and the angular shape of the rocks told him where the fish liked to wait. He had learned to read the river the way others read a book. When the rod bent again, he did not move.","zh":"天刚亮，那个垂钓的人就站在冰凉的河水里，端详着鱼线的角度。他知道，大鱼的分量会把鱼竿压成一道深深的弧。猛地一拽可能让小船朝一侧倾斜，所以他把双脚叉开，身子微微前倾。每次甩竿，都会把鱼钩送到芦苇边一处安静的空当，那里的水流几乎没有速度。鱼线顺流慢慢漂下去，岩石棱角分明的形状告诉他鱼爱在哪儿等。他已经学会像别人读书那样去读这条河。当鱼竿再一次弯下时，他没有动。"},"compose":{"tw":[["component",4],["write",0],["arrange",3],["plan",2],["improvise",6],["composure",4],["frame",0],["draw",3],["calm",2],["transcribe",6],["pen",0]],"en":"My sister likes to compose short songs on quiet evenings. She will write a few lines in her notebook with an old pen, then draw a rough frame for the melody. Her plan is never fixed, because she likes to improvise when a good idea comes. First she will arrange the notes of each component into a simple pattern, and then she will transcribe the whole piece onto paper. Once a tune is finished, she needs composure, a calm mind, before she can play it for us. Last winter she sat by the window and hummed until the room felt warm. The song was short, but it stayed with me for days.","zh":"我姐姐喜欢在安静的傍晚写点短曲子。她会用一支旧钢笔在笔记本上写几行，再为旋律画一个粗略的框架。她的计划从不固定，因为一有好点子她就爱即兴发挥。她先把每个组成部分的音符排成一个简单的样式，然后把整首曲子誊写到纸上。曲子一旦写成，她还需要镇定，一颗平静的心，才肯弹给我们听。去年冬天，她坐在窗边一直哼，直到屋里都让人觉得暖和。歌很短，却在我心里留了好几天。"},"conclude":{"tw":[["conclusion",4],["close",0],["find",3],["agree",2],["outcome",6],["conclusive",4],["reason",0],["settle",3],["end",2],["resume",6],["resolve",0]],"en":"After three long evenings the small committee had to conclude its talks about the old park. On the first night nobody could find a reason to agree, and the meeting came close to a shouting match. By the second week the members began to settle on one plan, and the outcome looked brighter. The chair said they needed one conclusive vote before the end of the month. There was a short break, then they would resume the discussion. In the final conclusion they chose to keep the trees and repair the gate. It was a quiet resolve, made without anger. Everyone walked home under the same dark sky.","zh":"连着三个晚上，这个小委员会总算要给老公园的事作个结论了。头一晚，谁也找不出一个理由去赞成，会议差点吵起来。到了第二周，委员们开始对其中一个方案达成一致，结果看着亮堂了些。主席说，月底前必须有一次能定论的投票。中间歇了一会儿，然后他们要继续讨论。最后得出的结论是：留着那些树，把大门修好。这是一个平静的决定，没有带着气。大家在同一片夜色下各自回了家。"},"consequence":{"tw":[["consequent",4],["issue",0],["matter",3],["significance",2],["inevitable",6],["consequential",4],["moment",0],["train",3],["significant",6],["effect",0]],"en":"The flood that winter was a direct consequence of years of careless building. A consequent loss of farmland was the first thing the council had to face. The issue had great significance for every family near the river. Experts said such damage was inevitable once the old drains were blocked. A train line south of the town was cut for two weeks, and the effect on trade was severe. For a moment people wondered if anyone would take the matter seriously. Then a significant sum of money was promised for new walls. Every choice made that spring proved consequential for years to come.","zh":"那年冬天的洪水，是多年来草率建房直接造成的后果。随之而来的农田损失，是市政会首先要面对的事。这个问题对河边的每一户人家都意义重大。专家说，旧排水沟一堵，这样的损失就不可避免。镇南的一条铁路线被切断了两周，对买卖的影响很严重。有一阵子，人们在想究竟有没有人会把这件事当回事。随后，修新堤坝的一笔不小的钱被许诺下来。那年春天作出的每个选择，事后证明都在往后许多年里影响深远。"},"content":{"tw":[["contain",4],["subject",0],["experience",3],["limit",2],["discontent",1],["material",6],["message",0],["offer",3],["satisfy",2],["alternative",6],["capacity",0]],"en":"The content of the course surprised everyone on the first day. It did not contain long lists of facts, and there was no fixed limit to what we could read. The subject was hard, but the teacher drew on her own experience in the field. Some students felt discontent at first, because they wanted easy answers. She would offer them a simple alternative: work in pairs and talk. The material was thin, yet the message was strong. To satisfy our questions, she let each group choose its own small task, and the room had more than enough capacity for it. By the end, most of us had changed our minds.","zh":"这门课的内容第一天就让大家吃了一惊。里面没有一长串事实，我们能读什么也没有固定的限度。这个科目很难，可老师靠的是自己在这行里的亲身经历。起初有些学生心里不痛快，因为他们想要现成的答案。她给他们提了个简单的替代办法：两人一组，开口聊。材料很单薄，传达的意思却很有力。为了满足我们的疑问，她让每组自选一个小任务，而教室的容量绰绰有余。到最后，我们大多数人都改了看法。"},"commission":{"tw":[["commit",4],["charge",0],["board",3],["crime",2],["council",6],["committee",0],["jury",3],["order",2],["panel",6],["mission",0]],"en":"The town council set up a commission to look into a serious crime at the port. A small committee was chosen, and a panel of three experts was asked to join. Their mission was clear: find the facts, not a name to blame. The board gave them the power to call any witness. A jury would later decide the case in court, but that was a different job. The chair read each charge aloud and asked the members to commit to a fair report. No one knew how long the order would hold. The work began the next morning, quietly.","zh":"镇议会成立了一个委员会，来调查港口上的一桩重案。他们挑了一个小小组，还请三位专家组成一个小组。他们的使命很清楚：找出事实，而不是找一个背锅的名字。董事会授权他们传唤任何证人。陪审团过后会在法庭上裁决，但那是另一回事。主席把每一项指控念了出来，要求成员们承诺交出一份公正的报告。没人知道这道命令能维持多久。第二天一早，工作就悄悄开始了。"},"convert":{"tw":[["conversion",4],["change",2],["break",3],["replace",2],["allow",6],["convince",0],["dress",3],["score",2],["obtain",6],["exchange",0]],"en":"Last year my cousin decided to convert an old barn into a small music room. The conversion took six months, and almost everything had to change. Workers had to break down two inner walls and replace the roof. She needed permission to allow a new window, and it took weeks to obtain it. Her brother did not believe the plan would work, so she had to convince him with drawings. On the first evening she would dress the room with old posters and a wooden bench. A young singer came to try the space and left a short score on the table. It was, in the end, a fair exchange: a barn for a studio.","zh":"去年，我表姐决定把一座旧谷仓改成一间小音乐室。这次改建花了六个月，几乎什么都得变。工人得拆掉两堵内墙，再把屋顶换掉。她需要许可才能开一扇新窗，光办下来就花了好几周。她哥哥不信这计划能成，她只好用图纸去说服他。头一晚，她用旧海报和一张木凳把屋子布置起来。一个年轻歌手来试了试场地，在桌上留下了一张短乐谱。到头来，这也算一笔公道的交换：一座谷仓换一间工作室。"},"convention":{"tw":[["convene",4],["normal",0],["mores",3],["assembly",2],["forum",6],["rule",0],["treaty",2],["congress",6],["pattern",0]],"en":"Every year an assembly of small nations will convene in the same quiet town. The convention lasts a week, and the usual pattern is always the same. A forum is held in the morning, and in the afternoon each group works on its own text. It is normal for the talks to be slow; no one expects a quick answer. The local mores of the town, like shaking hands and sharing tea, help the guests relax. By the last day the leaders hope to sign a treaty, though not every rule pleases every side. A large congress often ends without a single clear promise. Still, the guests come back, year after year, and talk again.","zh":"每年，一批小国都会在同一座安静的小镇开大会。这场会议持续一周，惯常的程式总是老样子。上午设一个论坛，下午各组各自斟酌自己的文本。谈判进展慢是常事；谁都不指望很快有答案。小镇上的风气——比如握手、一起喝茶——让客人们放松下来。到最后一天，各国领导人希望能签一份条约，虽说并非每条规则都让各方满意。大型的代表大会常常结束得连一句明确的承诺都没有。可客人们还是一年一年地回来，接着谈。"},"abstract":{"tw":[["lift",0],["absolute",3],["see",2],["concrete",1],["expressionist",6],["hook",0],["right",3],["steal",2],["contemporary",6],["outline",0]],"en":"In the gallery there was a room of abstract work that few people understood. On one wall hung a large canvas by a contemporary painter, all bright lines and no clear shape. Next to it was a rough expressionist study in heavy black and red. A guard said a thief had once tried to steal the smallest piece, using a long hook. Now the owner would not lift the painting from its place. The price was absolute: no offers, no trade. Visitors had to see the outline first and the color later, he said. To the right stood a plain concrete wall, and it held the whole room together.","zh":"画廊里有一间展厅，摆着很少有人看得懂的那些抽象作品。一面墙上挂着一幅当代画家的大画，尽是鲜亮的线条，没有明确的形状。旁边是一张粗犷的表现主义习作，浓重的黑与红。一名保安说，从前有个贼想用一根长钩把那幅最小的画偷走。如今主人再也不肯把那幅画从原位挪开。价钱是定死的：不还价，不交换。他说，看的人得先看轮廓，再看颜色。右边立着一堵素净的混凝土墙，正是它把整间屋子撑在了一起。"},"administration":{"tw":[["administer",4],["governance",0],["polity",3],["medication",2],["policy",6],["administrative",4],["bush",6]],"en":"Deep in the bush a small clinic depends on the local administration. The staff must administer medicine to families who travel for a whole day to reach them. Good governance is not an idea here; it means the right medication arriving before the rains. A new policy from the town promised more money for rural care. The head nurse had to fill in long administrative forms each month. She often said that a polity is judged not in the capital but in a village like this. When the road is cut, only a small boat can reach the clinic. Nobody in the room likes to think about that.","zh":"丛林深处有一个小诊所，全靠当地行政部门撑着。工作人员得给走上整整一天才赶到的家庭发药。在这里，好的治理不是一句空话；它意味着对的药赶在雨季前送到。镇上新出的一项政策，答应给乡村医疗多拨些钱。护士长每月都要填一沓长长的行政表格。她常说，一个政体的好坏，不看首都，而看这样一个村子。路一断，就只有一条小船能开到诊所。屋里没人愿意去想这件事。"},"communicate":{"tw":[["pass",0],["ask",3],["transfer",2],["excommunicate",1],["understand",6],["convey",2],["carry",3],["interact",2],["inform",6],["transmit",0]],"en":"Every Sunday the small church would communicate its news by hand. A young helper would carry each note to the homes near the gate. Older members liked to ask before they would interact, and some could not understand why the priest would not excommunicate anyone. 'A letter can convey more than a shout,' he said. He would pass the paper down the row and let people transfer it to a neighbour. Words, he believed, were meant to inform and to transmit a little warmth. He never wanted them to push a soul out into the cold. That habit kept the whole village close.","zh":"每个星期天，那座小教堂都要靠人手把消息传出去。一个年轻帮手会把每条便条送到大门口附近的人家。年长的成员总要先问一声才肯与人往来，有些人想不通，神父为什么从不把谁赶出教门。他说，'一封信比一声吼更能传递东西。'他会把纸条顺着长凳往下传，让人们转给旁边的邻居。他相信，话是用来告知的，也是用来送一点暖意的。他从不愿让一句话把谁推到冷风里去。就这一条习惯，把整个村子拢得很近。"},"confine":{"tw":[["hold",2],["ground",3],["control",2],["free",1],["starve",6],["limit",0],["pound",3],["decrease",2],["detach",6],["restrain",2]],"en":"The small pound would confine lost dogs until an owner came. Workers had to hold each animal still and check its health. They tried to control the noise with soft music, and they never let a dog starve. A narrow room could limit how many could stay, so the number had to decrease in busy weeks. One old dog would ground itself in a corner and refuse to move. To detach a frightened animal from its cage took patience and a gentle hand. Kind words, not force, were used to restrain a shaking dog. In the end most of them went home to a family, free at last.","zh":"那个小小的收容所会把走失的狗关起来，直到主人找来。工作人员得把每只动物按住，检查它的身体。他们试着用轻音乐压住叫声，从不叫一只狗饿着。房间窄，能收留的数量有限，所以忙的时候数目就得降下来。有一只老狗会把自己趴在角落里，死活不肯动。要把一只受惊的动物从笼子里弄出来，得有耐心和一双温柔的手。安抚一只发抖的狗，靠的是好话，不是蛮力。最后它们大多回了家，终于自由了。"},"cease":{"tw":[["cessation",4],["end",2],["break",3],["truce",6],["finish",0],["drop",3],["resume",6],["stop",0]],"en":"After two days the heavy rain finally began to cease. The town had waited for that cessation with growing worry, watching the river rise. A short truce between the two sides at the works also helped, and a break in the storm let them repair the pipes. Workers would stop only for a quick meal, then resume their long shift. They hoped to finish the wall before the water came again. Every hand made the rain drop a little less frightening. When the sky cleared, the whole street seemed to breathe. That was the end of a hard week, and no one wanted another like it.","zh":"两天之后，大雨终于开始停了。全镇怀着越来越重的心等这场雨停下，眼看着河水上涨。工地两边短暂的停战也帮了忙，趁风暴喘口气的工夫，管道得以修补。工人们只停下来匆匆吃口饭，又接着上长班。他们盼着赶在水再涨之前把堤墙修完。人人出一把力，那雨落下来也就没那么可怕了。天放晴时，整条街仿佛都松了一口气。艰难的一周就此结束，谁也不想再来一回。"},"characteristic":{"tw":[["character",4],["feature",0],["external",3],["property",2],["pattern",6],["streak",3],["quality",2],["trait",6]],"en":"The old teacher had one clear characteristic that everyone remembered. It was not a matter of looks or any external feature; it was the way she listened. Kindness was a trait she shared with her whole family, and it showed in the pattern of her daily work. Patience was another quality, a steady streak that never seemed to break. People said her true character came out when a student was in trouble. Good teaching, she believed, was a property of the heart, not of the voice. She never spoke of it herself. That silence was, perhaps, her finest feature of all.","zh":"那位老教师身上有一个谁都记得的鲜明特点。这跟长相或任何外在的东西无关；那是她倾听的方式。善良是她和全家共有的一种品质，从她日常做事的章法里就能看出来。耐心是她的另一种品质，一条稳稳的、好像从不断掉的脉络。大家都说，学生遇上难处时，她真正的品性才显出来。她相信，好的教学是一种心里的质地，而不是嗓音的质地。她自己从不提这些。那份沉默，或许才是她最动人的地方。"},"code":{"tw":[["codify",4],["encrypt",0],["address",3],["tag",2],["system",6],["access",3],["encode",2],["standard",6]],"en":"A young programmer had to write code that would encrypt every message. Before she could begin, she had to codify the old rules into a short list. Each address on the network needed a tag, and the whole system had to follow one standard. She would encode the name of every user so no outsider could read it. Only a manager had access to the master key. A good code is easy to keep and hard to break, she said. The team tested it for a week without a single fault. Then they let it run on the town network.","zh":"一位年轻程序员要写一段代码，把所有信息都加密。动手之前，她得先把那些旧规矩整理成一张短短的清单。网络上的每个地址都要有个标签，整套系统也得遵循同一个标准。她要把每个用户的名字都编码，让外面的人读不出来。只有主管才有权拿到那把总钥匙。她说，好的密码好用，难破。团队测了一个星期，没出一点毛病。随后就让它跑在镇上的网络上。"},"constitution":{"tw":[["constitute",4],["formation",0],["structure",3],["property",2],["statute",6],["makeup",0],["texture",3],["congress",6]],"en":"After a long struggle the people wrote their first constitution. The statute said that three regions would constitute one nation, and that a congress would meet each year. Its structure was simple: rights first, duties second. A special texture of the soil also mattered, because the farmers of the south wanted their land protected. The makeup of the assembly was fair to every district. In time the law became a property of the whole people, not of one group. Many who had helped to write it never saw its formation complete. Yet it held.","zh":"经过漫长的斗争，这些人写下了他们的第一部宪法。法典里写明，三个地区共同构成一个国家，每年召开一次国会。它的结构很简单：先讲权利，后讲义务。南边泥土那种特别的质地也重要，因为南方的农民想要他们的土地受到保护。议会的人员构成对每个区都算公道。时间一长，这部法律成了全体人民的东西，而不是某一群人的。许多帮着起草它的人没能看到它完全成形。可它立住了。"},"correspond":{"tw":[["correspondent",4],["fit",0],["meet",3],["equal",2],["differ",6],["match",0],["square",3],["analogous",6]],"en":"The editor asked me to check that two lists correspond before we went to press. The names in one column did not fit the numbers in the other, and the totals would never meet. Two figures were equal, but the rest seemed to differ by a little. I had to match each name with its own line and to square the sum at the bottom. A foreign correspondent sent a report with an analogous problem, and we laughed about it on the phone. In the end the mistake was small and easy to fix. The page came out clean that night.","zh":"编辑让我核对两份名单是否对得上，然后才付印。一栏里的名字跟另一栏的数字对不上，合计数怎么也算不平。有两个数相等，其余的似乎都差那么一点。我只得把每个名字跟它那一行配起来，再把底下的总数算准。一位驻外记者发来一篇稿子，也碰上差不多的麻烦，我们在电话里笑了半天。到头来那个错很小，也好改。那天夜里，版面清清爽爽地出来了。"},"abandon":{"tw":[["empty",0],["expose",3],["leave",2],["persuade",6],["desert",0],["chuck",3],["discard",2],["negotiate",6],["vacate",0]],"en":"When the last factory in our street closed, my uncle had to vacate the flat above it. He did not want to leave the empty rooms, but the owner would not negotiate. My aunt tried to persuade him to desert the place sooner rather than later. We helped him chuck old boxes and discard papers he had kept for years. One broken window exposed the cold to the whole floor. He said the town had abandoned its workers long before, and that no promise had ever held. We carried the last box out and locked the door behind us.","zh":"我们这条街上最后一家工厂关门后，叔叔不得不腾出楼上那套房子。他舍不得离开那些空荡荡的房间，可房东不肯商量。婶婶劝他早些弃了这地方，别再拖。我们帮他扔掉旧箱子，丢开他攒了多年的纸张。一扇破窗把寒气透进整层楼。他说这座镇子早就抛弃了它的工人，什么承诺都没兑现过。我们抬出最后一只箱子，反手锁上了门。"},"absorb":{"tw":[["draw",0],["involve",3],["interest",2],["emit",1],["reduce",6],["engage",0],["assimilate",3],["moisture",6],["suck",3]],"en":"The new panels on the roof absorb sunlight all day, and they also draw heat from the air. The manager said the system would reduce the power we buy from the grid and emit almost nothing. It can suck moisture out of a damp wall and then release it outside. Our old buildings slowly assimilate this new technology. The whole project does involve some risk, and it had to engage the workers for a month. At first the plan did not interest anyone, but the numbers won them over. We watched the meter turn and felt calm.","zh":"屋顶上的新板子整天吸收阳光，也从空气里吸取热量。经理说这套系统能减少我们从电网买的电，还几乎不排放什么。它能把湿墙里的水汽吸出来，再排到室外。我们的老房子慢慢地把这种新技术同化进来。整个项目确实有风险，工人们为此忙了一个月。起初这主意谁也不感兴趣，可数字说服了他们。我们看着电表转，心里很平静。"},"abuse":{"tw":[["shout",0],["curse",3],["treat",2],["step",0],["fracture",3],["use",2],["criminal",6],["insult",0]],"en":"At the old workshop the manager began to abuse his power. He would shout at anyone who was slow, curse the machines, and insult a young worker in front of the others. One day the boy tried to step back, fell, and the doctor found a small fracture in his wrist. The union said the man had no right to treat people that way. He only used his rank to frighten them. In court he was called a criminal, and the judge said such abuse ruins a whole team. The workers hoped the case would teach other managers a lesson.","zh":"在那间老作坊里，经理开始滥用他的权力。谁动作慢他就嚷，骂机器，还当众辱骂一个年轻工人。有一天那男孩想往后退，摔倒了，医生在他手腕上发现一处小骨裂。工会说这人没有权利那样对待别人，他不过是借职位吓人。法庭上他被称作罪犯，法官说这样的虐待会毁掉整个班组。工人们希望这案子能给别的经理一个教训。"},"accommodate":{"tw":[["admit",0],["quarter",3],["change",2],["capacity",6],["fit",3],["seat",3],["meet",2],["build",6],["hold",0]],"en":"Workers had to build a new hall to accommodate the winter market. Its capacity is three hundred, and one seat can hold two full baskets. Last year we had to change the plan twice because the old room could not fit so many people. The mayor would not admit the space was too small until the first fair. A quarter of the sellers had to meet outside in the cold rain. Now the wide new roof covers them all and keeps the rain out. It is a simple building, but it fits the town.","zh":"工人们得建一座新会堂来容纳冬季集市。它的容量是三百人，一张座位能放下两篮货。去年我们只好两次改动方案，因为那个旧屋子挤不下这么多人。镇长直到第一次集市才肯承认地方太小。四分之一的摊主只能在冷雨里在外面碰头。如今宽大的新屋顶把他们全罩住了，也挡住了雨。这是一座简朴的房子，却合这座小镇的用。"},"accompany":{"tw":[["company",0],["rule",3],["play",2],["send",6],["follow",0],["run",3],["travel",2],["prepare",6],["companion",0]],"en":"Every spring my sister asks me to accompany her on a long train trip to the coast. The company pays for the tickets, and there is one simple rule: we must travel light. On the way she likes to play cards, and I usually follow her lead. The train will run all night, so we prepare a small bag of food. She is a quiet companion, and I enjoy her company. This year she wanted to send a card to everyone at home before we left. We sat by the window and watched the fields go by.","zh":"每年春天，妹妹都要我陪她坐长途火车去海边。车票由公司出，规矩只有一条：行李要轻。一路上她喜欢打牌，我多半跟着她的节奏走。火车要开一整夜，所以我们备了一小包吃的。她是个安静的同伴，我也喜欢有她作陪。今年她想在出发前给家里的每个人寄一张卡片。我们靠着车窗坐着，看田野一片片过去。"},"alert":{"tw":[["alarm",0],["wake",3],["signal",2],["monitor",6],["awake",0],["horn",3],["warn",2],["precaution",6],["brisk",0]],"en":"The night guards must stay alert beside the old forest. A small alarm rings if the wind turns, and a horn on the tower can wake the whole village. A screen helps them monitor every dry hill. The first signal of fire often comes after midnight, when everyone is not yet awake. They warn the farmers by radio and take every precaution they can. A brisk walk around the fence is part of the night. Last summer a single spark started a small fire, and their quick answer saved the fields. Now nobody sleeps without one ear open.","zh":"守夜人得在古老的林子旁保持警觉。风一转向，一只小警报器就会响；塔上的号角能把全村人唤醒。一块屏幕帮他们监视每一座干枯的山丘。火的第一道信号往往在午夜以后出现，那时谁还没醒。他们用无线电提醒农户，能做的防备都做了。绕着围栏快走一圈是夜里的一部分。去年夏天一粒火星引燃了一小片火，他们反应快，救下了田。如今没有人不竖着一只耳朵睡觉。"},"amend":{"tw":[["better",0],["build",3],["change",2],["repeal",6],["improve",0],["help",3],["correct",2],["approve",6],["repair",0]],"en":"The club had to amend its old rules after a long meeting. We wanted to improve the way we share the field and to change the sign about late fees. The head said we could build a better system if we worked together. She would not approve the new list until every line was correct. Two members asked to repeal the rule about fines, but we kept it. Some small repairs to the changing room helped everyone. In the end the whole plan was better than before, and we voted it through. It was not a big change, but a real one.","zh":"开完一个长会，俱乐部决定修订它的旧章程。我们想改进共用场地的方式，也想改掉那块关于逾期费的告示。会长说，只要大家齐心，就能建一套更好的办法。她不肯批准新名单，除非每一行都正确。有两名成员要求废止关于罚款的那条，我们保留了下来。更衣室的一些小修小补帮了所有人的忙。最后整份方案比原先更好，我们投票通过了。这算不上大改动，却是实实在在的一次。"},"assault":{"tw":[["round",0],["jump",3],["knock",2],["raid",6],["attack",2],["rip",3],["battle",2],["weapon",6],["outrage",0]],"en":"Late that night there was an assault near the bus stop, and the news spread fast. A man tried to knock a young rider down and rip a bag from her hand. She fell on the second round of shouts. A passing driver jumped out and blew the horn. The police said the attack was not planned, and they found no weapon. It was not a battle, only a sad act between two angry people. The public felt outrage, and the town asked for more light on the street. Officers promised a raid on the empty lots nearby.","zh":"那天深夜，公交站附近发生了一起袭击，消息传得很快。一个男人想把一个年轻骑车人打倒，从她手里扯走一只包。在第二阵叫喊里她摔倒了。一位开车路过的司机跳下来，按响了喇叭。警方说这次攻击并非预谋，也没找到凶器。这不是一场打斗，只是两个愤怒的人之间的一桩惨事。公众很愤慨，镇里要求在街上多加照明。警员答应清查附近那片空地。"},"assemble":{"tw":[["meet",3],["club",3],["join",2],["prepare",6],["piece",0],["crowd",3],["interact",2],["reassemble",6],["gather",0]],"en":"Every Sunday the model club meets to assemble a new machine from old parts. First we gather all the pieces on a wide table and prepare a simple plan. New members can join at any time and interact with the older ones. It takes hours to put each small part in place; if we make a mistake, we must reassemble the whole frame. Sometimes a crowd of children comes to watch. We stop to meet their questions and show them how the parts fit. By evening one small car stands on the table, and the club goes home happy.","zh":"每周日，模型社的人聚在一起，用旧零件拼装一台新机器。先把所有零件摊在一张大桌上，定一个简单的方案。新成员随时可以加入，和老成员一起配合。每个小零件归位都要好几个钟头；一出错，整副框架就得重装。有时一群孩子会来看。我们停下来回答他们的问题，给他们演示零件怎么装。到了晚上，桌上立起一辆小车，大家高高兴兴地回家了。"},"assess":{"tw":[["tax",0],["rate",3],["charge",2],["ensure",6],["measure",0],["grade",3],["determine",2],["assure",6],["value",0]],"en":"Each spring the office must assess the land before it sets the tax. Workers measure every field and determine its true value. They give each farm a grade, then set a fair rate for the year. The team has to ensure that no one is charged twice. The owner asked them to assure him that the numbers were right. In the end the tax came lower than he feared. He signed the paper, thanked the clerk, and walked home slowly. 'A fair measure,' he said, 'saves us all a quarrel.'","zh":"每年春天，这间办事处都得在定税之前评估这些地。工作人员丈量每一块田，判定它真正的价值。他们给每个农场定一个等级，再定下当年公道的税率。这队人必须确保没有谁被重复收费。农场主请他们保证数字没错。最后税额比他担心的还低。他签了字，谢过办事员，慢慢走回了家。他说，'量得公道，我们就省了一场争吵。'"},"assign":{"tw":[["attribute",0],["allow",3],["choose",2],["instruct",6],["designate",0],["post",3],["appoint",2],["evaluate",6],["portion",0]],"en":"On Monday the manager had to assign the summer jobs to six students. She would instruct each one and then post a list on the wall. She chooses two to garden and designates a third as the driver. The head office had to appoint a team leader, and they picked a quiet boy. Each person received a small portion of the work, no more than they could handle. Later she would evaluate every task and attribute the good results to the team. She did not allow any idle hours. By Friday the list was full and the office was calm.","zh":"周一，经理得给六个学生分配暑期的工作。她先逐个交代，再把名单贴在墙上。她挑两个人去管园子，指派第三个当司机。总部还得任命一个组长，他们选了一个不爱说话的男孩。每人分到一小份活，不超过能担得起的量。之后她要评定每一项任务，把好成绩归功于这个团队。她一分钟闲工夫都不许有。到周五，名单排满了，办公室里很安静。"},"beam":{"tw":[["air",0],["burn",3],["express",2],["horizontal",6],["send",0],["tie",3],["feel",2],["surface",6],["shine",0]],"en":"A thin beam of light crossed the dark room and touched the wall. It came from a small lamp that would burn all night. The surface of the water below began to shine. The beam was almost horizontal, and it seemed to send a long thread through the air. My father used a rope to tie the lamp so it would not fall. He said the light could express more than any word. In the morning we could feel the warmth on the floor. It had been a quiet, beautiful test.","zh":"一道细细的光柱穿过昏暗的屋子，照到墙上。它来自一盏会亮一整夜的小灯。下方水面的光开始闪亮。这道光几乎是水平的，像是往空气里送出长长的丝线。父亲用绳子把灯拴住，免得它掉下来。他说这光能表达的东西比任何话都多。到了早上，我们能在地板上感到那股暖意。这是一次安静而漂亮的试验。"},"bid":{"tw":[["call",0],["double",3],["attempt",2],["deal",6],["offer",2],["order",3],["seek",2],["stake",6],["play",2]],"en":"At the auction my uncle made one careful bid for an old wooden desk. He did not want to play a risky game, so he would not double his offer. A man in the back made a second attempt and won with a higher stake. The clerk had to call the final price twice. It was a good deal for a desk of that age. Later my uncle would seek a chair to match it. He said he had learned one thing: never order a piece you have not seen. We carried the desk home in the rain.","zh":"拍卖会上，叔叔为一张旧木桌谨慎地出过一次价。他不想玩冒险的把戏，所以不肯把报价翻倍。后排一个男人又试了一次，用更高的赌注拿下了它。办事员只好把最后的价钱喊了两遍。那个年份的桌子，这算一笔好买卖。后来叔叔还想找一把椅子来配它。他说他记住了一件事：没亲眼见过的物件，千万别订。我们冒着雨把桌子抬回了家。"},"blast":{"tw":[["blow",2],["pump",3],["cut",2],["explosion",6],["fire",2],["puff",3],["experience",2],["bomb",6],["shoot",0]],"en":"In the old quarry a single blast could be heard across the valley. The workers would pump air into a deep hole, then light a small charge. The blow shook the ground, and a puff of grey dust rose over the trees. It was not an explosion like a bomb, they said, but a slow cut into the stone. My father had years of experience with such work and knew the risk. He would not let anyone shoot near the fence. After the fire was out, they waited, then checked the wall again. The valley was quiet once more.","zh":"在那个老采石场，一声爆破能传遍整个山谷。工人们先往深孔里打气，再点着一小包炸药。气浪震动了地面，一团灰白粉尘升到树梢之上。他们说，这不是炸弹那样的爆炸，而是往石头里慢慢切一刀。父亲干这种活有多年经验，知道其中的危险。他不许任何人在围栏附近开炸。火灭之后，他们又等了一阵，再检查了一遍石壁。山谷重又静了下来。"},"boost":{"tw":[["further",0],["carry",3],["push",2],["increase",6],["rise",0],["feed",3],["raise",2],["bolster",6],["advance",0]],"en":"The small shop needed one good week to boost its sales before winter. The owner would push the new coats to the front and raise the old prices down. A short notice in the local paper helped bolster the whole plan. Sales began to rise after the first cold day. She had to feed the workers lunch and carry boxes herself. The increase in trade was small but real, and it gave her the money to advance the second shop. A little further, she said, and the year would be safe.","zh":"这家小店入冬前需要有一个好星期来提振销量。老板娘把新外套推到最前面，把旧价钱往下降。本地报纸上一则小启事给整个计划添了把力。第一个冷天过后，销量开始回升。她得管工人午饭，还得自己搬箱子。生意多出来的那点不多，却是真的，让她有钱去推进第二家店。她说，再往前一步，这一年就稳了。"},"border":{"tw":[["edge",2],["lip",3],["touch",2],["northern",6],["ring",0],["shore",3],["supply",2],["eastern",6],["frame",0]],"en":"Along the border of our garden runs a low stone wall. At its edge stands an old tree, and near the lip of the path we planted small flowers. The eastern side touches the road, while the northern part meets a fence. My mother put a metal ring around each young plant to keep the birds away. The wall has become a supply of stones for every small repair. From the shore of the little lake you can see the whole frame of the house. It is a plain garden, but we love it.","zh":"我们花园的边上有一道矮矮的石墙。墙头立着一棵老树，小路的口子旁边，我们种了些小花。东边挨着马路，北边接着一道围栏。母亲给每株幼苗套了一个金属圈，防鸟来啄。这道墙也成了修修补补时取石头的来源。从小湖岸边，你能望见整座房子的轮廓。这是个普普通通的花园，我们却很爱它。"},"boundary":{"tw":[["edge",3],["end",3],["line",2],["parallel",6],["limit",3],["margin",3],["extent",2],["section",6],["bounds",0]],"en":"The two farms share one long boundary, and every year they walk it together. The line runs from the edge of the wood to the end of the field. A dry stream lies parallel to it for a while. The owners argue about the exact limit near the old stone, where the margin is not clear. No one knows the full extent of the land on paper. This section belongs to both, they agree. They put small marks along the bounds and shake hands. It is a simple way to keep the peace.","zh":"两个农场共用一条长长的地界，每年他们都会一起走上一遍。这条线从林子边一直到田的尽头。一条干涸的小溪有一阵子与它平行。在靠老石头的地方，边线不清，两位主人就为确切的界线争执起来。纸面上，谁也说不清这块地到底有多大。这一段两家都算，他们同意了。他们沿着界边做了些记号，握了握手。这是个维持和睦的简单法子。"},"broadcast":{"tw":[["air",0],["carry",3],["message",2],["radio",6],["programme",0],["interrogate",3],["sow",2],["channel",6],["send",0]],"en":"Every morning the farm radio can broadcast a short programme about the weather. The station will air it before the sun is up and carry it across the valley. Farmers turn the channel to hear whether they should sow that day. The host may interrogate a guest about the best time to plant. Then she will send one clear message to every village. The signal travels through the air and reaches even the far hills. My old grandfather never misses it even once. He says the small radio is his best worker.","zh":"每天早上，农场的收音机都会播一小段天气预报。电台会在太阳出来之前播出，把声音传遍整个山谷。农户拧到那个频道，听听当天该不该下种。主持人有时会追问一位客人，什么时候种最好。然后她会给每个村子送去一句清楚的话。信号穿过空气，连最远的山丘也收得到。我年迈的爷爷一次都不肯漏听。他说这台小收音机是他最好的帮手。"},"campaign":{"tw":[["cause",0],["war",3],["advertise",2],["dole",6],["drive",0],["reform",3],["race",2],["support",6],["fight",0]],"en":"The town began a quiet campaign to clean the river bank. A small group would advertise the day in every shop and ask for support from the farms. The drive was simple: one bag for each visitor. My aunt said it was a fight against years of waste, though no war was ever declared. She also wanted a reform of the old bins near the market. Some families on the dole came to help for free. The race to fill the most bags made everyone laugh. By noon the cause had a hundred hands, and the bank looked new.","zh":"镇里发起了一场清净河岸的安静运动。一小拨人挨家店铺张贴日子，也向农场求援。办法很简单：每位来的人拿一个袋子。婶婶说，这是跟多年的垃圾打一场仗，虽然从没宣过战。她还主张改一改市场边上那些旧垃圾桶。几家领救济的人也来白帮忙。比比谁装得多的那场竞赛把大家都逗笑了。到中午，这件事已经有上百双手，河岸看着像新的一样。"},"cancel":{"tw":[["scratch",0],["strike",3],["balance",2],["postpone",6],["offset",0],["recall",3],["remove",2],["announce",6],["delete",0]],"en":"The airline had to cancel our morning flight because of the storm. They would announce the news at the gate and help us postpone the trip to Friday. I had to delete two bookings from my phone and remove an old note. The clerk said the company would offset the cost with a small refund. A scratch on my old ticket hardly mattered then. The office would recall the seats and put them back on sale. We tried to balance our plan with the weather. In the end one quiet strike of luck kept us calm.","zh":"因为暴风雨，航空公司只好取消我们早上的航班。他们会在登机口公布消息，帮我们把行程改到周五。我只得从手机里删掉两个订票，再撤掉一条旧备忘。办事员说公司会用一小笔退款来冲抵损失。那时我那张旧票上的划痕已经无所谓了。售票处会把座位收回，再重新上架。我们尽量在天气和计划之间找个平衡。到最后，一点小小的运气让我们保持了镇定。"},"capture":{"tw":[["catch",0],["bag",3],["change",2],["attempt",6],["charm",0],["carry",3],["assume",2],["enemy",6],["entrance",0]],"en":"A young photographer waited all morning to capture the first light on the lake. Her only attempt was to catch the moment when the birds left the water. She would change her lens and carry a heavy bag through the wet grass. The charm of the place made her forget the cold. At the entrance of the old hut she met a man who called himself her enemy in the contest. She could only assume he was joking. One click, and the picture was there. It was, she said, the best shot of the year.","zh":"一位年轻摄影师守了一上午，想捕捉湖上的第一缕光。她唯一的尝试就是抓住鸟儿离水的那一刻。她要换镜头，还要背着沉沉的包穿过湿草地。这地方的美让她忘了冷。在旧小屋的门口，她遇到一个自称是她比赛对手的人。她只能当他是在开玩笑。咔嚓一声，照片就成了。她说，这是今年最好的一张。"},"chill":{"tw":[["cool",0],["ice",3],["change",2],["drizzle",6],["shiver",0],["quench",3],["fear",2],["cold",6],["thrill",0]],"en":"A sharp chill came with the evening wind, and we began to shiver by the fire. The weather had changed from a warm day to a cool night in one hour. A thin drizzle fell on the tent, and the ice on the small lake grew hard. We drank hot tea to quench our thirst and chase away the cold. My brother said the fear of the dark was worse than the wet. Still, there was a thrill in the wild air. We pulled our coats close and watched the stars. In the morning the sun warmed everything again.","zh":"一阵刺骨的寒意随晚风而来，我们靠着火堆开始发抖。天气一个小时里就从暖日变成了凉夜。细密的雨丝落在帐篷上，小湖上的冰也冻硬了。我们喝热茶解渴驱寒。弟弟说，对黑暗的害怕比身上湿更难受。可这荒野的空气里仍有一种刺激。我们把外套裹紧，看星星。到了早上，太阳又把一切晒暖了。"},"circulate":{"tw":[["circle",4],["drift",3],["run",2],["percolate",6],["spread",3],["loop",3],["travel",2],["condense",6],["broadcast",0]],"en":"A strange story began to circulate through the whole school. It would spread from one class to the next before noon. Someone said the water in the old pipe could percolate up through the floor and make a small circle of damp. A rumour like that can travel fast and loop back on itself. My teacher had to broadcast a calm note to every room. She said the report should not condense into fear. The truth would run its own course. By evening the story had begun to drift away, and the halls were quiet again.","zh":"一个离奇的说法开始在全校流传。不到中午它就从一间教室传到下一间。有人说旧水管里的水会渗上地板，渍出一小圈潮湿。这样的传言跑得飞快，还会绕回来。老师只好向每个教室发一条镇定的通知。她说，这消息不该凝成恐惧。真相自会走自己的路。到了傍晚，那个说法开始散去，走廊又安静了。"},"cluster":{"tw":[["bunch",0],["knot",3],["form",2],["contain",6],["bundle",0],["huddle",3],["meet",2],["compound",6],["flock",0]],"en":"A cluster of small birds settled on the fence by the field. They would huddle together whenever the wind rose, like a tight knot of feathers. Each bunch would form a warm bundle on the wire. The whole flock seemed to contain one mind, moving as a single shape. Farmers often meet such groups in winter, when the grain is low. The birds would then reach a small compound of trees and wait for the light. My sister watched them from the gate. She said they looked like a family on a cold morning.","zh":"一小群小鸟落在田边的栅栏上。风一起，它们就挤成一团，像一簇紧紧相扣的羽毛。每一伙都在铁丝上团成一个暖暖的包袱。整群鸟仿佛只有一个心思，移动起来像同一个形状。冬天谷粒少的时候，农夫常碰到这样的鸟群。它们会飞到一小片树丛里，等着天亮。妹妹从大门边看着它们。她说它们像寒冷早晨里的一家人。"},"collapse":{"tw":[["break",3],["pop",3],["change",2],["demise",6],["burst",0],["shock",3],["fold",2],["wake",6],["crack",0]],"en":"After weeks of rain the old wall began to collapse, and the sound made us wake at dawn. A long crack had run across it, and one stone could break free at any moment. We heard a sharp pop, then the whole top seemed to fold. It was not a burst like a bomb, just a slow fall. The shock of it changed my uncle's plan for the garden. He said the demise of the wall was a lesson about water. Nobody was hurt, and that was luck. We spent the day moving good stones to the shed.","zh":"下了几个星期的雨，那堵老墙开始倒塌，响声把我们在天亮时惊醒。一道长裂缝横在上面，随时可能有一块石头崩开。我们听见一声脆响，接着整个墙顶像是折了下来。它不像炸弹那样爆开，只是缓缓塌下。这场震动改变了叔叔修园子的打算。他说这堵墙的覆灭是关于水的一课。没人受伤，算是走运。我们花了一整天，把好石头搬到棚子里去。"},"combat":{"tw":[["fight",0],["shock",3],["conflict",2],["force",6],["battle",2],["rumble",3],["contend",2],["military",6],["scrap",0]],"en":"All spring the village had to combat the rising river. The fight began when the water reached the lower road, and a long conflict started between farmers and the council over the new wall. The town used every force it had: old trucks, sand, and strong arms. It felt like a small battle, with no soldiers and no military order. We could hear the rumble of stones under the bridge. Two groups would contend for the best spot to pile the bags. There was not a scrap of dry land left near the bank. After a week the river fell, and the shock slowly left us.","zh":"整个春天，村子都得跟上涨的河水搏斗。河水漫到下面那条路时，这场斗争就开始了，农民和镇议会也围绕新修的墙起了长期的冲突。镇里把所有力气都用上了：旧卡车、沙土，还有膀子。那阵仗像一场小仗，却没有士兵，也没什么军事调度。我们能听见桥下石头滚动的轰响。两拨人争抢堆放沙袋的好位置。河岸边没有留下一丁点干地。一个星期后河水退了，那种惊悸也慢慢散去。"},"compound":{"tw":[["combine",0],["fan",3],["add",2],["simple",1],["mortar",6],["heighten",0],["mix",3],["whole",2],["fire",6]],"en":"In the old kitchen my aunt would combine flour and water to make a simple paste. The whole recipe is a compound of three cheap things. First she would mix them well, then add a little salt to heighten the taste. A small fan in the corner kept the fire low. She used a heavy stone mortar to crush the grain into powder. The result was not fancy, but it held everything together. My brother said it tasted better than any shop food. We ate the whole pot before noon.","zh":"在那间老厨房里，婶婶会把面粉和水和在一起，搅成一种简单的糊。整份配方不过是由三样便宜东西合成的混合物。她先把它们拌匀，再加一点盐把味道提起来。角落里的小风扇把火压得低低的。她用一只沉重的石臼把谷粒捣成粉。做出来的东西并不讲究，却能把一切都黏住。弟弟说它比店里任何吃食都香。还没到中午，我们就把一整锅吃光了。"},"conflict":{"tw":[["difference",0],["war",3],["state",2],["strife",6],["fight",3],["assault",3],["contrast",2],["ongoing",6],["battle",0]],"en":"The conflict over the water began as a small difference between two farms. What started as a quarrel grew into a long battle, though no real war was ever declared. The state sent two men to help them talk. Each side could point to the contrast between their old rights and the new rule. The fight had been ongoing for three seasons. One night there was even an assault on a fence, which frightened the children. In the end a quiet neighbour found a way to share the stream. The strife faded, and both families began to plant again.","zh":"这场用水之争，起初只是两个农场之间的一点分歧。一场口角慢慢变成长期的争斗，虽然从没真正宣过战。上面派了两个人来帮他们谈。两边都可以指指自己旧有的权利和新规矩之间的反差。这场架已经持续了三个季节。有天夜里甚至有人动了围栏，把孩子们吓得不轻。最后一位安静的邻居想出了共用水溪的办法。纷争淡了下去，两家又开始下种。"},"conserve":{"tw":[["husband",0],["jam",3],["save",2],["waste",1],["absorb",6],["maintain",0],["jelly",3],["replenish",6],["preserve",2]],"en":"Every autumn my grandmother would conserve the fruit from her garden. She would make a thick jam and a clear jelly, and to husband the sugar she used only a little. We had to save every clean jar and never waste a single spoon. The old cupboard would absorb the smell of fruit for weeks. She liked to preserve the taste of summer for the cold months. In spring she would replenish the shelves with new glass. Her tap was simple, but it helped maintain the whole kitchen. We spread the last jar on bread in March.","zh":"每年秋天，奶奶都会把园子里的果子做成果酱保存起来。她会熬一罐稠稠的果酱和一罐清亮的果冻，为了节省糖，只用一点点。我们得把每个干净的罐子都留着，一勺也不许浪费。旧橱柜会把果香吸进去，好几周都散不掉。她喜欢把夏天的味道留到冷天里。到了春天，她再用新罐子把架子补满。她的法子很简单，却能让整间厨房运转下去。三月里，我们把最后一罐抹在面包上。"},"construct":{"tw":[["build",0],["law",3],["trace",2],["complex",6],["manufacture",0],["lock",3],["speculate",2],["project",6],["fabricate",0]],"en":"Engineers had to construct a new bridge over the busy road. They would build it in two parts to keep the traffic moving. The design was complex, and every line had to follow the law. The team would manufacture the steel beams far away and then bring them by truck. One worker could trace each beam back to its own number. The new lock on the gate kept strangers out. Some people would speculate that the project would cost twice the plan. In the end, the men did not fabricate a single claim; the bridge stood on time.","zh":"工程师们得在繁忙的马路上面建一座新桥。为了不堵住车流，他们分两截来造。设计很复杂，每一条线都得合乎规范。钢梁在很远的地方制好，再用卡车运来。有个工人能把每根梁都按编号追溯回去。大门上装了新锁，外人进不来。有人猜测这项工程的花费会翻倍。到头来，工人们并没有编造任何说法；桥按时立了起来。"},"contend":{"tw":[["deal",0],["box",3],["act",2],["say",6],["fight",3],["meet",3],["claim",2],["blame",6],["manage",0]],"en":"Two young runners had to contend for the last place on the team. On rainy days they would box on the old mat to warm up, then fight for every step in the final race. Each would act as if the other were a wall to pass. Their coach had to manage both and keep the peace. He would meet them after training to deal with the quarrel. One boy said that luck, not skill, had decided the race, and he began to blame the judge. The other made a quiet claim about his own hard work. In the end both ran, and both smiled.","zh":"两个年轻跑者要为队里最后一个名额一争高下。下雨天他们会在旧垫子上对打几下热身，然后在决赛里为每一步拼命。两人都像是把对方当成一堵要越过的墙。教练得管住两个人，维持住和气。训练后他会把他们叫到一起，处理这场争执。一个男孩说，定胜负的是运气不是本事，还开始怪裁判。另一个则平静地说起自己下的苦功。到最后，两个人都上了场，也都笑了。"},"crop":{"tw":[["dress",0],["top",3],["bear",2],["harvest",6],["work",0],["drift",3],["cut",2],["maize",6],["clip",0]],"en":"In the field the maize crop stood taller than my father. The top of each plant would bear two heavy ears of grain. All summer he had to work the soil and cut away the dry leaves. When the harvest came, the whole family helped to clip the stalks and carry them in. My mother would dress in her oldest clothes for the dust. A warm wind made the pollen drift across the rows. In autumn they brought the crops down the hill on one cart. It had been a good year for the farm.","zh":"地里的玉米比我父亲还高。每株顶端都会结两穗沉甸甸的谷子。整个夏天他都得翻土、剪掉枯叶。收成的时候，全家都来帮忙剪秆、搬回去。母亲会换上最旧的衣服，怕沾灰。暖风把花粉吹过一排排庄稼。秋天，他们用一辆车把收成运下山。对这座农场来说，这是个好年景。"},"crush":{"tw":[["beat",0],["cheat",3],["break",2],["revenge",6],["press",2],["stamp",3],["change",2],["fight",6],["jam",0]],"en":"To make the drink my sister had to crush a handful of soft berries. She used a heavy press to break the skin and let the juice run out. The pulp would jam the small grid, so she had to work slowly. My brother wanted to beat the mixture by hand to save time. He tried to cheat by adding sugar, but she caught him, and he wanted revenge with a joke of his own. She would stamp the lid shut with her foot and change the cloth twice. It was not a fight, only a lesson about patience. In the end we all got a glass.","zh":"为了做那杯饮料，妹妹得把一把软浆果压碎。她用一副重压榨器把果皮挤破，让汁流出来。果肉会堵住那层小滤网，所以她只能慢慢来。弟弟想用手快速搅匀省时间。他偷偷加糖想蒙过去，被妹妹抓住了，他就想开个玩笑报复一下。她用脚把盖子踩实，又换了两回布。这不是吵架，只是一堂关于耐心的课。最后我们每人都分到了一杯。"},"curve":{"tw":[["cut",0],["wave",3],["line",2],["loop",6],["wind",0],["bow",3],["shape",2],["angle",6],["bend",0]],"en":"The road began to curve along the coast, and the sea came into view. A long line of white wave broke on the stones below. At one angle the path would bend left, then loop back toward the hills. We had to cut a corner where the wind was strong. My sister made a quick bow as the wind pushed her hat off. The shape of the bay, she said, was like a wide smile. We left the main road and took a slow way home. It was the best part of the trip.","zh":"公路沿着海岸拐起弯来，大海也映入眼底。一道长长的白浪拍在下面的石头上。在一个角度上，小路向左一弯，又绕回山里。风大的地方我们抄了个近道。一阵风把妹妹的帽子吹掉，她急忙鞠了一下身。她说，这海湾的形状就像一张咧开的笑脸。我们离开大路，慢慢往家走。这是这趟旅行里最好的部分。"},"cycle":{"tw":[["round",0],["ordinary",3],["pass",2],["phase",6],["wheel",0],["recycle",3],["rate",2],["slow",6],["bike",0]],"en":"Every day my cousin rides her bike to work through the park. It is an ordinary trip, but she likes the even cycle of the pedals. Each wheel turns a full round and carries her past the trees. In the wet phase of spring she rides at a slow rate. Her family tries to recycle old paper and glass every week. She says a good day should pass without any hurry. The same small ride, over and over, brings her a quiet joy. It costs nothing and keeps her strong.","zh":"每天，堂姐都骑自行车穿过公园去上班。这是一段寻常的路，可她就喜欢蹬踏的那种匀称循环。每个轮子转满一圈，带着她经过一棵棵树。春天湿漉漉的那段时间，她骑得慢些。她家每周都尽量回收旧纸和玻璃。她说，好日子就该不慌不忙地过去。这一趟趟重复的小路，给了她一份静静的快乐。它不花钱，还让她身体结实。"},"advocate":{"tw":[["advocacy",4],["counsel",0],["propose",2],["staunch",6],["urge",2],["liberal",6],["preach",0]],"en":"My neighbour has been a firm advocate for the small village library for ten years. She would urge the council to keep it open and often had to preach patience to the young readers. Her advocacy was quiet but staunch, and she would never give up. She would propose a new plan at every meeting and offer free counsel to anyone who asked. Some called her too liberal with the town money, but she only smiled. Last spring the library got a new roof. 'Books wait,' she said, 'and so can we.'","zh":"我邻居为村里那间小图书馆奔走了十年，是个坚定的倡导者。她总去劝议会别把它关掉，还常常对年轻读者讲要耐心。她的主张不张扬，却很坚决，从不放弃。每次开会她都会提一个新方案，谁问她都愿意免费出主意。有人说她对镇上的钱太大方，她只是笑笑。去年春天，图书馆换了新屋顶。她说：'书会等，我们也等得起。'"},"belief":{"tw":[["believe",4],["impression",0],["religion",3],["idea",2],["faith",6],["notion",0],["contrary",6]],"en":"My old teacher had a firm belief that a good question is worth more than a quick answer. He did not follow any religion, yet he had a quiet faith in people. His first impression of a student often came from the eyes, not the marks. He would say that the common notion of a clever child was often quite contrary to the truth. His main idea was simple: believe nothing until you have tested it. On his last day he told us to keep asking. The whole class stood up and clapped.","zh":"我那位老教师有一个坚定的信念：一个好问题比一个快答案更值钱。他不信任何宗教，却对人抱着一份安静的信任。他对一个学生的第一印象往往来自眼睛，而不是分数。他常说，人们关于聪明孩子的普遍看法，往往与真相正好相反。他的核心想法很简单：没试过的东西，别去相信。最后一天他让我们继续发问。全班都站起来鼓了掌。"},"carbon":{"tw":[["carbonate",4],["charcoal",3],["paper",2],["nitrogen",6],["graphite",3],["copy",2],["hydrogen",6]],"en":"In the school lab we studied what a single element can do. Carbon is in the charcoal we burn, in the graphite of every pencil, and even in a sheet of paper. When it joins with hydrogen and nitrogen, it forms the gas that plants need, and with oxygen it becomes a carbonate in the sea. My partner had to copy the whole table from the board, line by line. She said the human body is mostly carbon too. That idea stayed with me all week. At home I checked the coal bag and found the same word written on it.","zh":"在学校实验室里，我们研究了一种元素能有多大本事。碳就在我们烧的木炭里，在每支铅笔的石墨里，甚至在一张纸里。它和氢、氮结合，就成了植物需要的气体；和氧结合，就变成海里的一种碳酸盐。我的搭档得把黑板上的整张表一行行抄下来。她说人体里也大部分是碳。这个想法在我脑子里留了整整一周。回到家我又去看了煤袋上的字，发现写的还是同一个词。"},"column":{"tw":[["columnist",4],["pillar",0],["atlas",3],["shape",2],["page",6],["article",2],["mail",6]],"en":"My cousin writes a weekly column for a small town paper. She is the only columnist who still walks to the office with a paper atlas under her arm. Her desk sits by a tall stone pillar near the window, and she likes the shape of the old room. Each page of her article has to be checked twice before it goes out. Readers send her mail from every village, and she answers them all. Last week a letter came from a farmer who said her words had kept his hope alive. She read it three times, then began the next piece.","zh":"我表姐给一家小镇报纸写每周专栏。她是唯一一个还夹着一本纸质地图册步行去上班的专栏作家。她的桌子紧挨窗边一根高大的石柱，她喜欢这间老屋子的形状。她那篇文章的每一页，发出去之前都得核对两遍。读者从各个村子给她寄信，她每封都回。上星期来了一封信，一个农夫说她的文字让他没丢掉希望。她读了三遍，然后开始写下一篇。"},"conceive":{"tw":[["concept",4],["consider",0],["discover",3],["replicate",6],["think",3],["feel",3],["procreate",6]],"en":"It is hard to conceive of a world where a machine can think like a person. My professor asked us to consider how the first idea of such a device came to someone. The concept began with a simple question: can a metal hand feel? To discover the answer, his team had to replicate the movement of a human arm, step by step. They could not procreate life, of course, but they could learn from it. He said the best work begins when you stop trying to copy and start to ask. I wrote that line in my notebook.","zh":"很难想象一个机器能像人一样思考的世界。教授让我们想想，这种装置最初的点子是怎么落到某个人头上的。这个概念起于一个简单的问题：一只金属的手能有感觉吗？为了找到答案，他的团队只好一步一步地模仿人手臂的动作。当然，他们没法造出生命，却可以向生命学习。他说，最好的工作开始于你不再照抄、开始发问的那一刻。这句话我记在了本子上。"},"accomplish":{"tw":[["reach",3],["run",3],["complete",2],["realise",6],["achieve",0],["average",3],["effect",2],["execute",0]],"en":"My team had one week to accomplish a task that usually takes a month. We had to run three tests a day to reach our goal in time. Most of us were only average at the work, but we stayed late. The plan was to complete the first part by Wednesday and then execute the second. We did not realise how tired we had become until Friday. In the end we did achieve what we set out to do, and the effect on the whole office was clear. The manager bought us all lunch.","zh":"我们组只有一个星期，去完成平时要一个月才干完的任务。为了按时达到目标，我们一天要跑三遍测试。我们多数人水平都只是中等，可都留下来加班。计划是周三前做完第一部分，然后执行第二部分。到周五我们才意识到自己已经累成什么样。最后我们真的做到了想做的事，整个办公室的气氛也明显不一样了。经理请我们大家吃了午饭。"},"ache":{"tw":[["hurt",0],["burn",3],["pain",2],["numb",6],["pine",0],["catch",3],["bruise",6],["smart",0]],"en":"After the long climb my legs began to ache, and a dull pain settled in my back. I had caught a small bruise on my knee when I slipped. At first the cut did not hurt much, but later it seemed to burn. My hand went numb from holding the cold rail, and I could not feel my fingers. The doctor said I should not pine for the top of the hill; rest would do more good. A smart choice, she said, is to stop before you fall. I sat by the fire and drank hot tea.","zh":"爬了那么久的山，我的腿开始疼，背上也闷闷地痛。我滑了一跤，膝盖上磕出一小块淤青。伤口起初不太痛，后来越来越像在烧。手扶着冰冷的栏杆，慢慢就麻了，指头都感觉不到。医生说我不该一心惦记着山顶，好好休息更有用。她说，聪明的做法是在摔倒之前先停下。我坐在火边，喝了几口热茶。"},"achieve":{"tw":[["reach",3],["average",3],["succeed",2],["aim",6],["accomplish",0],["score",3],["objective",6],["attain",0]],"en":"My aim this term was to reach a higher mark in maths. My teacher said that only a few students achieve their first goal, and I did not want to be average. I wrote my objective on a card and kept it on the desk. To succeed, I had to do one extra set of problems every night. It was slow, and I did not score well on the first test. But by June I managed to accomplish what I had set out to do and to attain the mark I wanted. My mother put the card on the wall.","zh":"这个学期我的目标是把数学成绩提上去。老师说，只有少数学生能实现最初的目标，而我不想只是个中等生。我把目标写在一张卡片上，放在书桌上。为了成功，我每晚得多做一套题。进步很慢，第一次测验考得也不好。可到了六月，我还是把当初想做的事做成了，也达到了想要的分数。我妈把那张卡片贴在了墙上。"},"adjust":{"tw":[["adapt",2],["address",3],["change",2],["dictate",6],["correct",0],["square",3],["balance",6],["align",0]],"en":"When we set up the new machine, we had to adjust it to the old room. The first step was to correct the height and align the two parts. We had to adapt the frame so it could square with the wall. My father would not let the rules dictate how he worked; he would address each small problem by hand. The change took a whole afternoon, and finding the balance was the hardest part. At last the machine ran without a sound. He stood back and smiled. It had been a good day in the workshop.","zh":"装这台新机器的时候，我们得把它调到适合这间老屋子。第一步是量准高度，把两个部件对齐。我们还得改一下机架，让它和墙对成直角。我爸不让规矩来指挥他怎么干活，每个小毛病他都亲手去处理。这一改动花了整个下午，最难的是找到那个平衡点。最后机器转起来一点声响都没有。他退后一步，笑了。作坊里，这一天过得不错。"},"aim":{"tw":[["drive",0],["address",3],["mean",2],["focus",6],["train",0],["charge",3],["plan",2],["effort",6]],"en":"My aim this year is to train for a longer race. I have to drive myself out of bed early and keep my focus on the plan. Some mornings it is hard to mean what I say about not quitting. The coach will charge a small fee for each class and give us a written plan. Every effort counts, he says, even the short runs. To address my weak knee, I do extra work on the stairs. In June I will see if the training was worth it. My sister says she will come and watch.","zh":"我今年的目标是练好一场长跑。我得逼自己早起，把注意力放在计划上。有些早上，我说自己不放弃的时候，自己都不太信。教练每节课收一点费用，还会给我们一份写好的计划。他说每一分努力都算数，哪怕只是短跑。为了应对我那只弱膝盖，我还在楼梯上多练。到六月，我就知道这些训练值不值了。我妹妹说她会来看。"},"alien":{"tw":[["foreign",5],["import",3],["change",2],["creature",6],["exotic",0],["exile",3],["transfer",2],["evil",6]],"en":"In the story I read, an alien lands in a quiet field and no one knows what to do. The creature is not evil, only foreign to everything here. The town must change its whole idea of a neighbour. Some want to import machines to study it, while others call it exotic and want a picture. The government plans to transfer it to a lab far away. A woman who lives alone offers it a home instead of exile. In the end the alien stays, and the village learns to say hello.","zh":"在我读的那个故事里，一个外来的生物落在一片安静的田野上，谁都不知道该怎么办。这东西并不邪恶，只是对这里的一切都陌生。镇上必须改变对'邻居'的整个想法。有人想进口机器来研究它，也有人觉得它稀奇，只想拍张照片。政府打算把它转到很远的实验室去。一个独居的女人却给它一个家，而不是让它被放逐。最后这个外来者留了下来，村子也学会了跟它打招呼。"},"aspect":{"tw":[["face",0],["side",3],["feature",2],["nature",6],["look",0],["surface",3],["countenance",2],["facet",0]],"en":"When I asked the old painter about a portrait, he said the hardest aspect is not the face but the light. Every side of a building has its own nature, and every surface tells you something. A good feature of a face, he said, is the small line near the eye. He would look at a person for a long time before he touched the paper. The countenance of a stranger can show more than a hundred words. Each facet of the work, he said, must be true. I watched him paint for a whole afternoon.","zh":"我问那位老画家画肖像最要紧的是什么，他说最难的一面不是脸，而是光。一栋楼的每一面都有自己的性子，每一个表面都会告诉你点什么。他说，一张脸上好的特征，是眼角那道细线。他总会盯着一个人看很久，才动笔。一个陌生人的神情，能说出比一百个字更多的东西。他说这幅画的每一个侧面都必须真实。我在那儿看他画了一下午。"},"assert":{"tw":[["insist",2],["assure",3],["declare",2],["argue",6],["maintain",0],["claim",3],["reassert",6],["affirm",0]],"en":"At the meeting my colleague began to assert that the new plan would fail. He would insist on his numbers and argue with anyone who disagreed. He had to declare his position early, then maintain it for an hour. Others would claim the opposite, and the room grew loud. The manager asked him to affirm just one point and to reassert it with proof. He could not, and finally sat down. Everyone in the room already knew exactly how he felt, and some of them smiled. He did assure us that he would bring better facts next time.","zh":"会上，我的同事开口就断言这个新方案会失败。他非要坚持自己的数字，谁不同意就跟谁争。他一上来就把立场亮出来，然后整整守了一个钟头。别人又声称正好相反，屋里越来越吵。经理让他只确认一个要点，再拿证据把它重申一遍。他做不到，最后坐了下来。在座的人早就清楚他是什么态度，有几个还笑了。不过他确实向我们保证，下次会带上更靠谱的事实。"},"award":{"tw":[["honour",0],["letter",3],["gift",2],["recipient",6],["present",0],["pension",3],["best",6],["grant",2]],"en":"Every year the town gives an award to the best young writer in each school. The recipient this year was a quiet girl who had never shown her work to anyone. She received a letter, a small gift, and a grant to buy books. To honour her, the head teacher read one page aloud. Her grandmother, who lives on a small pension, came in her best coat and cried a little. At the end the mayor would present a wooden cup. The girl said only thank you, and quietly sat down again.","zh":"每年镇上都会给各校最优秀的年轻作者一个奖项。今年的获奖者是个文静的女孩，她从没把自己的作品给任何人看过。她收到一封信、一份小礼物，还有一笔买书的资助。为了向她致敬，校长朗读了她的一页文字。靠一点养老金过日子的外婆穿上最好的外套来了，还掉了点眼泪。最后镇长要颁发一只木杯。女孩只说了声谢谢，又悄悄地坐下了。"},"bargain":{"tw":[["buy",0],["haggle",3],["agree",2],["stock",6],["deal",0],["purchase",2],["price",6],["steal",0]],"en":"At the market my mother loved to haggle over every price. She would buy the same things each week and never agree to the first number. Once she found a real bargain: a warm coat at half the usual price. She said it was almost a steal, and she would not leave it. The seller had a stock of old wool and wanted a quick deal. She made her purchase and walked away smiling. On the way home she told me the secret: never look too eager. That coat kept me warm for three winters.","zh":"在集市上，我妈最爱为每个价钱讨价还价。她每周都买同样的几样东西，从不答应第一个价。有一回她淘到了真正的便宜货：一件暖和的外套，只要平时一半的价钱。她说这几乎等于白捡，说什么也不肯放手。摊主积了一批旧羊毛，想快点做成一笔买卖。她付了钱，笑着走开。回家路上她告诉我诀窍：千万别显得太想要。那件外套让我暖和了三个冬天。"},"behave":{"tw":[["act",2],["deal",3],["hold",2],["interact",6],["bear",0],["follow",3],["ought",6],["carry",0]],"en":"The teacher told the new pupils that they ought to behave well in class. To follow the rule, they had to act with care and hold their tongues. A quiet girl would interact with the others by passing notes, which the teacher could not bear. One boy had to deal with a joke that went too far, and it was hard for him to carry on. She said that good manners are the way we show respect. At the end of the week the class was calmer. The teacher smiled for the first time.","zh":"老师对新来的学生说，在课堂上就该守规矩。要守这条规矩，他们做事得留神，还得管住自己的嘴。一个文静的女孩总传纸条跟别人来往，这让老师受不了。有个男孩不得不去处理一个开过头的玩笑，那阵子他很难撑下去。她说，好的教养就是我们表达尊重的方式。到周末，班里安静多了。老师第一次露出了笑容。"},"bias":{"tw":[["prejudice",2],["handicap",3],["partiality",2],["negative",6],["diagonal",0],["taboo",3],["gender",6],["preconception",0]],"en":"In our reading class we talked about bias in the news. A writer may show prejudice without knowing it, and a small partiality can turn a story negative. Our teacher said that a preconception about gender is one of the oldest of all. Sometimes the words run on a diagonal across the page, so the eye picks them first. Some papers treat a certain topic as a taboo that no one should touch. We had to find one example and explain it. My partner said a handicap of the writer is simply that no one is free of bias.","zh":"阅读课上，我们谈了新闻里的偏见。一个作者可能在不知不觉中就显出成见，一点点偏袒就能把一篇报道写得带着负面色彩。老师说，关于性别的成见是其中最早的一种。有时文字斜着排在页面上，眼睛会先看到它们。有些报纸把某个话题当成谁都不该碰的禁忌。我们得找一个例子来解释。我的搭档说，作者的一个短处就在于，没有人能完全摆脱偏见。"},"burden":{"tw":[["charge",2],["overwhelm",3],["concern",2],["reduce",6],["load",0],["pill",3],["risk",6],["weight",2]],"en":"When my grandmother fell ill, the care of the house became a heavy burden for my mother. She had to take on the extra charge of cooking and cleaning alone. The weight of it seemed to overwhelm her some evenings. Her main concern was that we children would be tired at school. To reduce the load, my sister and I took turns with the shopping. Our doctor said that a daily pill and less salt would lower the risk. Slowly the whole house felt lighter and warmer. My mother began to sleep again.","zh":"外婆病倒以后，操持这个家就成了我妈肩上很重的担子。做饭、打扫这些额外的活儿，全得她一个人扛。有些晚上，这份重量好像要把她压垮。她最担心的，是我们几个孩子在学校里累着。为了减轻负担，我和妹妹轮流去买东西。医生说，每天吃一片药、少吃点盐，能降低风险。慢慢地，家里轻松了些，也暖了些。我妈又开始睡得着了。"},"companion":{"tw":[["company",0],["date",3],["friend",2],["guide",6],["fellow",0],["consort",2],["mother",6],["associate",0]],"en":"For many years the old man's only companion was a thin brown dog. It would keep him company on the long walks and never leave his side. A young guide in the village became a good friend and would sometimes join them. He called the dog his fellow traveler and his quiet consort. One date in spring, his mother came to visit and brought a warm coat. An old associate from his working days also came by, and they talked for hours. The dog lay at their feet the whole time.","zh":"很多年里，老人唯一的伙伴就是一条瘦瘦的棕色狗。长途散步时，它总陪着他，从不离他左右。村里一个年轻的向导成了他的好朋友，有时也一起同行。他管那条狗叫他的同伴、他安静的伴儿。春天里的某一天，他母亲来看他，还带来一件暖和的外套。一位从前一起干活的老同事也来了，两人聊了好几个钟头。那条狗一直趴在他们脚边。"},"complex":{"tw":[["composite",5],["plant",3],["whole",2],["simple",1],["construct",6],["hybrid",3],["compound",5],["main",6]],"en":"The town built a new sports complex beside the old factory. The design was not simple: it was a composite of three buildings joined into one whole. To construct it, the workers used a hybrid of steel and wood. The main hall could hold four hundred people. Behind it stood a plant that made the ice for the rink. Every compound of glass and stone had to fit the ground exactly. On opening day the whole town came to look. Children ran from room to room, and no one wanted to go home.","zh":"镇子在老工厂旁边建了一座新的体育中心。设计并不简单：它是三栋楼拼成的一个整体。为了把它盖起来，工人们用了钢和木的混合结构。主厅能容纳四百人。它后面还有一座给溜冰场制冰的厂房。每一处玻璃和石头的组合，都得严丝合缝地对上地面。开放那天，全镇的人都来看。孩子们从一个房间跑到另一个房间，谁都不想回家。"},"conduct":{"tw":[["bear",0],["hand",3],["act",2],["exercise",6],["carry",0],["pose",3],["bring",2],["deal",3]],"en":"The way a person will conduct himself at a serious meeting tells you a lot. My teacher had to carry out the whole program without help. She would act as host and bring each guest to the front. A young man had to bear the load of the heavy boxes and to hand out the papers. She would pose a short question after every talk and deal with each answer kindly. She said the exercise was simple but made us brave. Everyone praised her calm conduct that day. I wrote down every word she said.","zh":"一个人在一场严肃的会议上的举止，能透露出很多。老师得一个人把整场活动操持下来。她既当主持，又把每位客人请到台前。一个年轻人得扛那些沉箱子，还要发材料。每段讲话后她都会提一个简短的问题，再耐心地回应每个答案。她说这项训练很简单，却让我们胆大了些。那天大家都夸她举止沉稳。她说的每句话我都记了下来。"},"confirm":{"tw":[["support",0],["back",3],["approve",2],["evidence",6],["affirm",2],["prove",3],["anonymity",6],["sustain",0]],"en":"Two separate tests had to confirm that the water in the well was safe. The first result was not enough, so the team looked for more evidence. A second study would support the finding and prove the point. The head of the lab had to approve the report before it went out. Some people asked for anonymity, because they feared trouble. A senior worker would affirm the numbers on paper and back the young team. The grant helped sustain the work for another year. After all this, the town could breathe again.","zh":"得有两份各自独立的检测来证实这口井的水是安全的。第一个结果不够，于是团队又去找更多的证据。第二份研究支持了这个结论，也把问题坐实。实验室的负责人得在报告发出去之前批准它。有些人要求匿名，因为怕惹麻烦。一位年长的员工会在纸上确认这些数字，还给这支年轻的团队撑腰。那笔资助让这项工作又维持了一年。折腾完这些，镇上的人总算能松口气了。"},"contradict":{"tw":[["oppose",0],["protest",3],["prove",2],["contrary",6],["contravene",0],["veto",3],["disagree",2],["clarify",6]],"en":"At the council meeting a young member stood up to contradict the old plan. Two reports seemed to prove the opposite, and the two sets of numbers seemed to disagree. She had to oppose the leader directly and even to veto one line. Her neighbour began to protest in a loud voice, saying the plan would contravene the law. Others said the contrary was true and the money was already spent. The chair asked both sides to clarify their points before the vote. I wrote down everything, because I could not decide who was right.","zh":"会上，一位年轻成员站起来反驳那套旧方案。两份报告似乎证明的正好相反，两组数字也对不上。她不得不直接反对领导，甚至否掉其中一行。她旁边的人开始大声抗议，说这方案会违反法律。另一些人说实情恰恰相反，钱早就花出去了。主席让双方在投票前把各自的要点讲清楚。我把全都记了下来，因为我实在分不清谁对。"},"coordinate":{"tw":[["organize",0],["structure",3],["manage",2],["facilitate",6],["align",0],["interlock",3],["meet",2],["initiate",6]],"en":"To organize the town festival, four groups had to coordinate their work for a month. One team would manage the stage, another the food stalls. A small office was set up to facilitate the daily talks. We had to align our times so that no two acts would meet. The wooden frames of the market had to interlock like a puzzle. The whole structure of the day was written on one big board. Each day began with a short meeting and one clear note. The leader said we should initiate nothing new until the old jobs were done.","zh":"为了筹办镇上的节庆，四个小组得协调配合一个月。一个队管舞台，另一个队管小吃摊。还设了个小办公室，方便每天对接。我们必须把时间对齐，免得两场演出撞在一起。集市的木架子要像拼图一样互相咬合。一整天的安排都写在一块大板上。每天开头都开个短会，只讲一件清楚的事。领队说，旧活儿没干完之前，别再开新头。"},"core":{"tw":[["centre",0],["stuff",3],["bar",2],["component",6],["heart",0],["chamber",2],["structure",6],["effect",0]],"en":"At the centre of the old factory stood a tall metal core. Inside it there was a narrow chamber where the hottest work was done. The main component was a thick bar that could bear great heat. The whole structure rested on that single part. Engineers said the stuff they used was the same as in a bridge. At heart, they said, the design was simple: one strong middle and many small pieces around it. The effect of that idea lasted for years. Later, other plants were built in the same way.","zh":"在老工厂的正中央，立着一根高高的金属核心。里面有一个狭窄的腔室，最热的一道工序就在那里做。最主要的部件是一根能承受高温的粗棒。整座结构都压在这一个部件上。工程师说，他们用的材料和造桥用的一样。他们说，这个设计说到底很简单：中间一根结实的柱子，周围一圈小零件。这个想法的影响持续了好多年。后来别的厂子也照这样盖。"},"corrupt":{"tw":[["buy",0],["load",3],["change",2],["criminal",6],["cloud",0],["poison",3],["pay",2],["spoil",0]],"en":"A newspaper story said that a manager in the water company had become corrupt. He would let a seller buy his signature with a heavy load of gifts. For years he took money to change the test results, and no one could stop him. He would pay a criminal to keep quiet about one bad pipe. Then a report began to cloud the whole office with doubt. The poison in the water had spoiled a whole street of gardens. In the end he lost his job and stood in court. The town never trusted that office again.","zh":"报纸上说，供水公司的一位经理变贪了。他由着一个供货商拿一大堆礼物买通他的签字。多年来他收钱篡改检测结果，谁也拦不住。他还花钱雇一个罪犯，对一根坏掉的管子闭口不提。后来一份报告让整个办公室笼上了疑虑。水里的毒物把整整一条街的花园都毁了。最后他丢了工作，站上了法庭。那座镇子从此再没信过那家事务所。"},"acknowledge":{"tw":[["admit",0],["confess",3],["accept",2],["notice",0],["sustain",3],["thank",2],["recognize",0]],"en":"When my paper was finally printed, I had to acknowledge the people who had helped me. I would admit that the first draft was weak, and I had to confess that a friend rewrote half of it. I could not accept all the praise alone. My teacher was the first to notice the small mistakes in the numbers. A neighbour gave me a room and enough quiet to sustain three long nights of work. In the last line I wrote down a list of names to thank. It is easy to recognize good work, but harder to share the credit for it.","zh":"当我的论文终于印出来时，我得向帮过我的人致谢。我愿意承认初稿很弱，也不得不坦白，有一半是一位朋友重写的。这份夸奖我不能一个人全收下。最先发现数字里那些小错的，是我的老师。一位邻居借给我一间屋子，还有足够的清静，让我撑过了三个长夜。在最后一行，我写下了一串要感谢的名字。认出好的成果不难，难的是把功劳分给别人。"},"affirm":{"tw":[["assert",0],["assure",3],["negate",1],["uphold",6],["confirm",0],["claim",3],["proclaim",6]],"en":"At the meeting the director had to affirm that the company would keep its promise. She would assert that no worker would lose a day of pay, and she tried to assure everyone that the plan was safe. A young clerk would negate that claim at once, saying the numbers did not fit. The board had to uphold the older rule and confirm the date of the next review. In front of the whole room the director then did something rare: she chose to proclaim the truth instead of hiding it. 'We were wrong,' she said. The workers said nothing, but the air changed.","zh":"会上，主管得明确表态，公司会守住自己的承诺。她断言不会有任何工人少拿一天的工资，还尽量让大家放心，说这个方案是稳妥的。一名年轻职员立刻否定了这个说法，说数字对不上。董事会只好维持原先的规矩，并确认下次复核的日期。当着满屋子的人，主管随后做了一件少见的事：她选择把真相讲出来，而不是藏着。'是我们错了，'她说。工人们什么也没说，可气氛变了。"},"anticipate":{"tw":[["expect",2],["act",2],["materialize",6],["promise",0],["happen",2],["prompt",6],["predict",0]],"en":"The old farmer taught me how to anticipate the weather before the harvest. He would expect a dry week and then act a day early, cutting the wheat while the sky was still clear. 'A promise from the clouds means nothing,' he said, 'so do not wait for rain to materialize.' It was hard to predict what would happen in the hills after noon. A single dark line on the horizon was enough to prompt him to call the whole family out to the field. We worked until dark. That year the storm came late, and we lost almost nothing.","zh":"那位老农教我怎么在收割前预判天气。他会料定有干旱的一周，然后提前一天动手，趁天还晴着把麦子割了。他说，'云一下子许下的诺，算不得数，别等着雨真的落下来。'过了中午山里会发生什么，很难预料。天边只要出现一条黑线，就足以催他把全家人都叫到地里去。我们一直干到天黑。那一年风暴来得晚，我们几乎没损失什么。"},"approximate":{"tw":[["guess",0],["reckon",3],["exact",6],["judge",0],["assess",3],["vary",6],["near",0]],"en":"The builder gave us an approximate price for the new roof. His first guess was six thousand, but he said the final cost would vary with the weather. A neighbour, who liked to reckon such things by eye, put the number much higher. We could not judge which was right without a careful look at the tiles. The surveyor came to assess the slope and the state of the old beams. His exact figure was very near the builder's first guess, though he asked for a small extra fee. 'An approximate answer is fine today,' he said. 'You can be sure of it later.'","zh":"包工头给我们报了个大概的新屋顶价钱。他头一回估算说是六千，但又说最终花销会随天气而变化。一位邻居爱凭眼力估这种数，报出的数高得多。不仔细看看瓦片，我们没法判断谁对。测量员来看坡度，也看那些老梁的状况。他给出的精确数字和包工头差得不多，只是多要了一小笔费用。'今天有个大概的数就够了，'他说，'以后再慢慢算准。'"},"attribute":{"tw":[["property",0],["shape",3],["derive",6],["assign",0],["space",3],["imply",6],["dimension",0]],"en":"The young engineer had to describe every attribute of the new plastic before it could be used. Its main property was that it stayed soft in the cold. She measured the shape and the exact dimension of each sheet, then checked how much space it would take in the package. A note in the file seemed to imply that the colour might change with age. She had to assign the testing work to two helpers and let them record the results. From those numbers she could derive a simple rule: thin sheets bend, thick ones hold. The design passed, and the factory ordered more.","zh":"这种新塑料能不能用，先得由那位年轻工程师把它的每一项特性都讲清楚。它最主要的特点是在低温下依然柔软。她量了每张板的形状和精确尺寸，又算了它在包装里要占多大地方。文件里的一句话好像在暗示，颜色可能会随着时间而变。她只好把测试的活儿分给两个帮手，让他们把结果记下来。从这些数据里，她得出了一条简单的规律：薄板会弯，厚板能撑。设计通过了，厂里又追加了订单。"},"ban":{"tw":[["censor",0],["embargo",3],["forbid",2],["impose",6],["injunction",3],["decree",2],["suspend",6]],"en":"Last year the city decided to ban thin plastic bags in every shop. The new decree would forbid them at the till and impose a small fine on anyone who broke the rule. Some owners asked the court for an injunction to delay the change, but the judges refused. The council also had to censor the worst ads of two stores that ignored the order. In the same month they placed an embargo on cheap plastic from abroad. Shops that kept using the old bags had their licence suspended for a week. Within a year, most shoppers carried their own cloth bags.","zh":"去年，这座城市决定在所有商店里禁止薄塑料袋。新的法令会禁止在收银台提供它们，还会对违规的人处以小额罚款。有些店主向法院申请禁令，想拖一拖这项改变，但法官没有同意。市政会还不得不审查两家无视规定的商店最过分的广告。同一个月，他们对国外来的廉价塑料实施了禁运。仍在用旧袋子的商店，执照被停了一周。一年之内，大多数顾客都自己带着布袋子了。"},"blend":{"tw":[["combine",0],["melt",3],["taste",6],["mix",2],["gauge",3],["mixture",6],["merge",0]],"en":"At the small tea shop the owner would blend three kinds of leaf for her morning cup. She liked to combine a strong dark tea with a light green one and then mix in a few dried flowers. The trick was to gauge the amount by eye, never by weight. If the water was too hot, the leaves would melt into a bitter mess. The final mixture had a soft taste that regular guests asked for by name. Over the years she would merge two old recipes into one and call it her house blend. 'A good cup,' she said, 'is a small argument that ends in peace.'","zh":"在那家小茶铺里，老板娘会用三种茶叶给自己调一杯早茶。她喜欢把浓重的红茶和清淡的绿茶配在一起，再掺进几朵干花。窍门是用眼睛估分量，绝不用秤。水要是太烫，茶叶就会化成一团发苦的东西。配好的混合物有种柔和的滋味，熟客都点名要它。这些年里，她把两个老配方合成一个，管它叫自家招牌。'一杯好茶，'她说，'就是一场最后归于平静的小小争论。'"},"charter":{"tw":[["rent",0],["contract",2],["mandate",6],["engage",0],["document",2],["extension",6],["hire",0]],"en":"The school could not afford to hire a bus for the trip, so they decided to charter one instead. The office had to sign a contract with a small local firm and read every line of the document first. The charter gave the driver a clear mandate to leave at six in the morning, even in the rain. It also allowed the school to rent two extra seats for parents. When the trip was delayed, the firm agreed to a short extension without a new fee. One teacher would engage a second driver so no one had to work all night. In the end twelve pupils and three adults climbed aboard.","zh":"学校出不起雇一辆大巴去旅行的钱，于是决定改成一整辆包租。办公室得和一家本地小公司签合同，还得先把文件上的每一行都看一遍。租约给了司机明确的授权：就算下雨，早上六点也要出发。它还允许学校多租两个座位给家长。行程往后推的时候，公司同意延长一小段时间，不再另收费用。一位老师又请了第二位司机，这样就没人得熬整夜。最后，十二名学生和三位大人上了车。"},"client":{"tw":[["customer",0],["patron",3],["computer",2],["file",6],["guest",3],["comment",6],["node",0]],"en":"A small design office was building a website for a new client, a shop that sold handmade lamps. The manager said this customer was the most patient they had ever had. Every evening a patron from the old art club would send a friendly comment on the first draft. The team kept a single file for all the notes, and each worker wrote to it from their own computer. One day the central node of their small network went down, and nobody could reach the pages for an hour. A special guest from another town came to watch the test and gave good advice. The client stayed calm and only asked for one more change.","zh":"一家小设计工作室在给一个新客户做网站，那是一家卖手工灯具的店。经理说，这位顾客是他们遇到过最有耐心的。每天晚上，一位老艺术协会的赞助人都会在初稿上留下一条友善的评论。团队把所有的备注都放在同一个文件里，每个人从自己的电脑上往里写。有一天，他们那个小网络的中心节点坏了，整整一个小时谁都打不开页面。一位从别的镇子来的特别客人看了测试，提了些好建议。客户始终很平静，只要求再改一处。"},"contest":{"tw":[["competition",2],["game",3],["oppose",2],["event",6],["contend",0],["race",3],["final",6]],"en":"The whole school entered a writing contest that year, and the final was held in the main hall. It was not a race of speed but a slow competition of ideas. Each pupil had to contend with the same hard subject: a day they would never forget. One class decided to oppose the rule that only older students could win a prize. The event lasted a whole afternoon, and parents filled the back rows. In the last game of words, a quiet girl read a short piece about her grandmother. The judges took a long time. She won, and no one in the room was surprised.","zh":"那一年全校都参加了一场写作比赛，决赛在礼堂里举行。这不是比谁快，而是一场慢慢比拼想法的较量。每个学生都得对付同一个难题：一个他们永远不会忘记的日子。有一个班决定反对那条只有高年级才能得奖的规矩。活动持续了整整一个下午，家长把后排都坐满了。在最后一场文字的过招里，一个安静的女孩念了一段写她祖母的短文。评委们斟酌了很久。她赢了，屋里没有一个人觉得意外。"},"contrast":{"tw":[["line",0],["oppose",3],["differ",2],["strong",6],["conflict",3],["distinguish",2],["less",6]],"en":"The teacher asked us to look at the contrast between two chairs in the workshop. They stood side by side, and a thin line of light fell between them. The two designs differ in almost every way, though both came from the same hand. One was strong and heavy, the other light and quick to break. We had to distinguish the real reason for the change, not just the look. It seemed to oppose everything the maker had said before, which caused a small conflict in the class. In the end the newer chair was less comfortable, and we all agreed on that.","zh":"老师让我们看作坊里两把椅子之间的差别。它们并排放着，中间漏下一道细细的光。这两个设计几乎处处不同，却出自同一双手。一把结实沉重，另一把轻巧、一碰就容易坏。我们得分辨出改动的真正原因，而不只是看外表。它好像跟这位匠人之前说的一切都对着来，班上因此起了小小的争执。到头来，新的那把椅子没那么舒服，这一点我们全都同意。"},"counsel":{"tw":[["advise",0],["tip",3],["message",2],["judge",6],["advocate",0],["warn",3],["associate",6]],"en":"Before the hearing, the lawyer had to counsel her client one last time. She would advise him to speak slowly and to answer only what was asked. A short tip helped more than a long speech: look at the judge, not at the floor. She sent the same message to his family, who were waiting outside. In the hall an older colleague, a strong advocate of fair trials, came to warn them that the other side would press hard. He was an associate of the firm and knew the case well. 'Say less,' he said, 'and let the facts do the work.'","zh":"开庭之前，律师得最后再给她的当事人一次忠告。她会劝他慢慢说，问什么答什么。一条短短的提示比长篇大论更有用：看着法官，别盯着地板。她把同样的话捎给了他等在外面的家人。走廊里，一位年长的同行——一个坚定的公平审判拥护者——过来提醒他们，对方会狠狠施压。他是事务所的合伙人之一，对这桩案子很熟。'少说两句，'他说，'让事实自己说话。'"},"curtain":{"tw":[["drape",0],["festoon",3],["blind",2],["roof",6],["mantle",0],["supply",2],["velvet",6]],"en":"My aunt spent the whole weekend making a new curtain for the front room. She chose a heavy velvet cloth and let it drape to the floor in soft folds. Her plan was to festoon the top with small rings so it would slide easily. The old blind by the window was grey, and the shop that used to supply them had closed years ago. High above, a thin mantle of dust covered the beam under the roof. She stood on a chair to reach it and laughed at the mess. When the curtain finally hung, the room felt ten years younger.","zh":"我姑妈整个周末都在给前屋做一幅新窗帘。她挑了块厚重的天鹅绒布，让它打着软软的褶子垂到地上。她的打算是在顶部缀上一排小环，好让它滑动起来更省劲。窗边那块旧遮帘已经发灰，过去供应它们的铺子几年前就关了。头顶高处，薄薄一层灰像披风似的盖在屋梁上。她踩在椅子上够到那儿，看着这一片狼藉笑了。等窗帘终于挂好，那间屋子像是年轻了十岁。"},"debate":{"tw":[["argue",0],["see",3],["controversy",6],["fence",0],["oppose",3],["issue",6],["contend",0]],"en":"Our class held a debate about whether the old field should become a car park. Two teams had to argue for and against the plan in front of the whole school. The issue had caused real controversy in the town for months. One student would contend that the children needed the space more than the cars did. The other side would oppose that view and point to the queue of vans every morning. 'You can see both points,' the teacher said, 'and that is why we talk.' At the end a few pupils sat on the fence, unwilling to choose. No vote was taken, but the room was quieter than before.","zh":"我们班就那块旧空地该不该变成停车场展开了一场辩论。两支队伍得当着全校的面对这个方案正反两边争。这件事在镇上已经争了好几个月，闹出了不小的议论。有个学生主张，孩子们比汽车更需要这块地方。另一方反对这个看法，指着每天早上排成队的货车。老师说：'两边的道理你都看得见，所以我们才要谈。'到最后，有几个学生骑在墙头上，谁也不肯选。没有投票，可屋里比之前安静了。"}}});
